15-The input after `--input` is split on ASCII whitespace.  A zero-length string is
16:an empty token stream.  Grammar terminals are single-quoted strings, such as
17-`'id'`, `'+'`, and `'\\''`; support backslash escapes for quote and backslash.
18:Nonterminals are identifiers beginning with an ASCII letter or underscore and
